  "question": {
    "text": "If three successive terms of a G.P. with common ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> are the length of the sides of a triangle and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>r</mi></mfenced></math> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to r, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>r</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to:"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>It is given that sum of any two sides is greater than the third side.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>Case-I: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Case-II: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is always true.</p><p>Case-III: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>∪</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Taking intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>r</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>r</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>r</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
  }
